# At least one of these is required.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional — auto-generated on first boot if left blank.
JWT_SECRET=

# Optional — defaults shown.
HTTP_PORT=8080
PG_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=systemprompt

# ── pi web terminal (the live agent on the homepage) ─────────────────────────
# Absent entirely unless SP_PI_GATEWAY_KEY is set: /api/public/pi/* 404s and no
# child-process machinery is built. Install pi first:
#   npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent
#
# Must be a PAT (sp-live-…), NOT an admin JWT: a JWT pins its own session_id
# claim, and each conversation attests a fresh session, so the gateway rejects
# the mismatch. Mint one with: POST /admin/devices/pats
#
# ⚠ Only the account that owns this PAT can actually drive the agent. Every
# conversation sends the session id attested for *its* user, and the gateway
# 401s a session belonging to anyone else. Until a per-conversation PAT lands,
# the homepage terminal is live for that one account and degrades for everyone
# else. See the module docs in handlers/pi/mod.rs.
# SP_PI_GATEWAY_KEY=<PAT pi authenticates to /v1/messages with>
#
# pi is a `#!/usr/bin/env node` script, and the child is spawned with a cleared
# environment — so if pi lives under nvm, BOTH of these are required or the
# child dies at exec:
# SP_PI_BINARY=/home/you/.nvm/versions/node/v22.19.0/bin/pi
# SP_PI_CHILD_PATH=/home/you/.nvm/versions/node/v22.19.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
#
# ⚠ SP_PI_TOOLS defaults to `read`, enforced by pi itself. Do NOT widen it to
# bash/write/edit on a single-container deployment: pi ships no sandbox, so
# that turns this into a remote code execution service. The governance chain
# gates intent, not blast radius. Widening needs a container per session.
# SP_PI_TOOLS=read
#
# Put the workspace root on a size-capped tmpfs in production.
# SP_PI_WORKSPACE_ROOT=/tmp/systemprompt-pi-sessions
#
# Caps and timeouts (defaults shown).
# SP_PI_MAX_PER_USER=1
# SP_PI_MAX_TOTAL=8
# SP_PI_IDLE_SECS=600
# SP_PI_MAX_LIFETIME_SECS=3600
# SP_PI_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_SECS=120
#
# Child resource ceilings. Only FSIZE is on by default — see config.rs:
# RLIMIT_NPROC counts every process the *uid* owns rather than the child's
# descendants, and needs bash (dash has no `ulimit -u`); RLIMIT_AS kills V8 at
# startup unless measured. Both are worth setting once the child has its own uid.
# SP_PI_RLIMIT_FSIZE=67108864
# SP_PI_RLIMIT_NPROC=0
# SP_PI_RLIMIT_AS=0
